Diagram: what happens when you type https://www.google.com and press Enter

  [Browser]
     |
     | 1. DNS resolution: www.google.com ?
     v
  [DNS resolver] -> [Root] -> [.com TLD] -> [Authoritative DNS]
     |
     | answer: IP address of www.google.com
     v
  [Browser]
     |
     | 2. TCP connection to the server IP on port 443
     | 3. TLS handshake -> the traffic is ENCRYPTED (HTTPS)
     v
  +--------------------------------+
  | FIREWALL (allows port 443)     |
  +---------------+----------------+
                  |
                  v
  +--------------------------------+
  | LOAD BALANCER (HAProxy)        |
  | distributes the request        |
  +-------+----------------+-------+
          |                |
          v                v
  +---------------+  +---------------+
  | WEB SERVER    |  | WEB SERVER    |
  | (Nginx)       |  | (Nginx)       |
  | serves a web  |  | serves a web  |
  | page          |  | page          |
  +-------+-------+  +-------+-------+
          |                  |
          v                  v
  +--------------------------------+
  | APPLICATION SERVER             |
  | generates the web page         |
  +---------------+----------------+
                  |
                  | requests data
                  v
  +--------------------------------+
  | DATABASE (MySQL)               |
  +--------------------------------+

  The response goes back the same way, encrypted, to the browser.
